 "findings": [
  "Setup A carries the system: 57 of 330 trades (17%) produce +167.2R of +178.8R. Without its 3 best trades it still makes +67.6R and it was positive in 5 of 6 years (bootstrap P(not better than the rest) = 0.000).",
  "Setup B is 64 trades (19% of all entries) for +7.1R in total (-5.6R without its best 3). It occupies slots and risk budget for roughly zero edge; this is a hypothesis to test in the builder at portfolio level, not a rule change.",
  "Setup C is 209 trades (63% of all entries) for +4.6R in total (-21.3R without its best 3). It occupies slots and risk budget for roughly zero edge; this is a hypothesis to test in the builder at portfolio level, not a rule change.",
  "Disaster-stop and gap exits cost -30.5R. Those entries were stretched: 12.3% above MA50 vs 4.7% for normal exits, RVOL 2.12 vs 1.36.",
  "Returns are tail-driven: the top 5% of trades supply 68% of gross profit. Any filter that skips entries has to be judged on R kept, not on hit rate.",
  "Live window: 29 closed trades, -5.41R, PF 0.36. Drawing 29 backtest trades that could have closed inside a 69-day window gives a result this bad 36% of the time (PF this low: 21%): normal for a young book. Comparing against all backtest trades, long winners included, would say 5% and wrongly suggest something broke. Only 2 Setup A entries vs 5.0 expected (P = 0.10); the live book has mostly been fed the setups that earn ~0R in the backtest too.",
  "Entry-feature drift vs backtest: none significant after Bonferroni (p < 0.0045). The machine is buying the same kind of stocks.",
  "ML entry filter (keep top 50% by model score), purged annual walk-forward: take-all +171.1R vs ridge +158.7R (IC -0.113) and logistic +125.8R (IC -0.059). Status: rejected - stays record-only.",
  "Deflated Sharpe: the 5-year curve's Sharpe 1.42 gives DSR 0.91 at the registry's 19 trials; it drops below 0.95 at about 10 independent trials. This is before the survivorship look-ahead the simulation page already measures, which lowers it further."
